message: "If you use esTS in research or software, please cite it."
title: "esTS, a library for statistics extraction from texts in Spanish"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shkarin
    given-names: Sergey
    email: kouki.sergey@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/SergeyShk/esTS"
url: "https://sergeyshk.github.io/esTS/"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22924655
license: MIT
version: 0.4.0.dev4
date-released: 2026-09-24
keywords:
  - spanish
  - nlp
  - text statistics
  - readability
  - lexical diversity
  - lexical sophistication
  - stylometry
  - corpus linguistics
  - datasets
abstract: "esTS computes text statistics for Spanish: extraction of sentences, words and character N-grams, rule-based syllabification and stress, basic counts, readability formulas with the scales of their authors, lexical diversity measures, lexical sophistication by a frequency dictionary of Google Books Ngram, morphological and syntactic statistics on Universal Dependencies, cohesion in the manner of Coh-Metrix with the Spanish discourse markers, components that put them all on a spaCy pipeline, corpus measures (keyness, collocations, dispersion, concordances, stylometric distances, comparison of corpora), datasets (a corpus of Spanish literature and the frequency dictionary) and visualizations."
